            <ArticleTitle>Coronary heart disease in Aboriginal communities: towards a model for self-management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>300-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary heart disease (CHD) is one of the main causes of death and disability in the Aboriginal population, and is the major cause of the twenty-year gap in life expectancy of Aboriginal and non-Aboriginal Australians. This paper explores Aboriginal health in relation to CHD, and suggests self-management as a culturally acceptable therapeutic and sustainable ideology from which positive outcomes may be achieved.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
